$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure B for the synthesis of
substrate (1): 2–5 To a Schlenk tube (25-mL) were added Pd(PPh3)4 (114
mg, 0.1 mmol, 5 mol %), CsF (620 mg, 4 mmol, 2.0 equiv), CuI (38 mg, 0.2
mmol, 10 mol %) and substrate 3 (2 mmol). The mixture was closed by a
septum, purged by nitrogen gas for several times then the dry 1,4-dioxane
(8 mL) was injected into the mixture by a syringe and the mixture was
allowed to stir for 10 min; o-bromoiodoarene 4 (2.4 mmol, 1.2 equiv) was
then slowly injected into the mixture by a syringe. The septum was
removed and the Schlenk tube was sealed with cap; again quickly purged by
nitrogen gas for several times and move to oil bath and allowed to stir
at 60 °C for 5 h. The crude reaction mixture was diluted with 30 mL
CH2Cl2, filtered through a thin Celite pad to remove salt and
concentrated in vacuo. The residue was isolated through flash column
chromatography by using hexane and ethyl acetate as eluent. Compounds 1.
Compounds 1p, 1q, 1G and 1K were obtained according to this procedure.
3-(2-Bromophenyl)picolinonitrile (1p): According to the general procedure
B, Pd(PPh3)4 (114 mg, 0.1 mmol, 5 mol %), CsF (620 mg, 4 mmol, 2.0
equiv), CuI (38 mg, 0.2 mmol, 10 mol %),
3-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)picolinonitrile (0.46 g, 2
mmol, 1.0 equiv) and o-bromoiodobenzene (0.68 g, 2.4 mmol, 1.2 equiv)
were stirred in dry 1,4-dioxane (8 mL) at 60 °C for 5 h. Work-up and
purification by column chromatography (Hex/EtOAc = 93:7).
2-(3-Bromoquinolin-2-yl)benzonitrile (1q): According to the general
procedure B, Pd(PPh3)4 (114 mg, 0.1 mmol, 5 mol %), CsF (620 mg, 4 mmol,
2.0 equiv), CuI (38 mg, 0.2 mmol, 10 mol %),
2-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)benzonitrile (0.46 g, 2
mmol, 1.0 equiv) and 3-bromo-2-iodoquinoline (0.80 g, 2.4 mmol, 1.2
equiv) were stirred in dry 1,4-dioxane (8 mL) at 60 °C for 5 h. Work-up
and purification by column chromatography (Hex/EtOAc = 23:2). Product 1q
as a white solid (556 mg, 90%). New compound. mp: 117–118 °C; IR (KBr):
3056, 2951, 2226, 1941, 1830, 1580, 1483, 1455, 1438, 1402, 1361, 1127,
1069, 905, 764, 730, 692, 594, 542 cm-1; 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.53
(s, 1H), 8.14 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.82–7.76 (m, 3H), 7.72 (t, J = 7.8
Hz, 1H), 7.67 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.62 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.56 (t, J =
7.8 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (150 MHz, CDCl3): δ 155.1, 146.3, 143.5, 139.9,
133.0, 132.3, 130.5, 130.2, 129.6, 129.0, 128.7, 128.2, 126.6, 117.6,
116.5, 112.7; HRMS: C16H9BrN2 calculated 307.9949, found 307.9941.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, slow addition of arene stage 2, sealed tube used
