$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A mixture of 4-(6-bromoimidazo[1,2-a]pyrazin-8-ylamino) benzoic acid
ethyl ester (19g; 55.3 mmol), 3-aminophenylboronic acid hemisulfate
(13.3g; 72 mmol), tetrakis (triphenylphosphine) palladium (2.9g; 2.5
mmol), 1N aqueous sodium carbonate solution (166 mmol), and
dimethoxyethane (200 mL) is heated at reflux for 4 days. The mixture is
allowed to cool down to RT, treated with water (200 mL), and extracted
with ethyl acetate (4x l00mL). The extracts are washed with water (2x150
mL) and brine (1 x 100 mL), dried over magnesium sulfate, and evaporated
in vacuo. The residue is triturated with dichloromethane and diethyl
ether. 4-[6-(3- aminophenyl)imidazo[1,2-a ]pyrazin-8- ylamino ]benzoic
acid ethyl ester as a yellow solid (17g, 85% yield).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structure-Based Drug Design of RN486, a Potent and Selective Bruton's
Tyrosine Kinase (BTK) Inhibitor, for the Treatment of Rheumatoid
Arthritis
